WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.460
- Have you ever thought to yourself,

00:00:01.460 --> 00:00:03.800
Damn, I have way too many friends.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:05.300
I am so popular.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.810
I need to start getting rid of people.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:07.820
Well, in this tutorial,

00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:09.910
I'm going to teach you
how to make everybody

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:12.210
you know and love slowly
drift away from you

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:13.510
over the course of your life.

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:14.490
Step number one,

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:16.970
talk almost exclusively about yourself.

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:18.940
You wanna develop a strong tendency

00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:23.060
to steer any conversation
back to the topic of yourself.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.190
What do you have going on?

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.080
What are your dreams and aspirations?

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.080
What are you excited about?

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:29.280
What's something shitty that
happened to you last weekend?

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.140
If you really wanna make talking to you

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.040
an agonizing experience,

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.740
then you really want to
monologue about yourself

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:37.000
as much as possible.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.400
And don't ask questions
about the other person.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.420
Be the one who answers questions.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:42.930
You don't ask questions.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:45.300
Do not under any circumstances,

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.660
give people the impression
that you are interested

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:50.763
in them or what they
have going on whatsoever.

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:53.600
How's it going, man?

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:54.440
- Hey, hey,

00:00:58.467 --> 00:00:59.680
I've been better.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:02.350
My grandpa just died actually.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:03.183
- Grandpa.

00:01:03.183 --> 00:01:04.016
- Yeah.

00:01:04.016 --> 00:01:04.849
- We were really close,

00:01:04.849 --> 00:01:06.840
and it's like the first
death in the family.

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:08.370
So it kind of hit me hard.

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:09.640
- Yeah damn man.

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:11.100
Yeah, my grandpa's super healthy.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.350
We're really happy about that.

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:14.320
And yeah, he's 78.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:15.530
He just like ran a marathon.

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:17.483
It's like really, really cool to see.

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:22.020
Yeah, like man grandpas
are so awesome sometimes.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.520
Listen, can we borrow
your truck on Friday?

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:25.480
Tip number two.

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:26.720
Talk about other people.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:29.900
Now, obviously you can't talk
about yourself the whole time.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:32.430
You might wanna sprinkle in
a little bit of detraction

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:33.263
while you're at it.

00:01:33.263 --> 00:01:35.470
Talk about mutual friends or acquaintances

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:37.470
in the most negative light possible.

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:40.660
Voice your dissatisfaction
and your disapproval

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:44.030
of their behaviors, their
life choices, their outfits.

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:46.510
You want to generally
give people the impression

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:48.780
that you're not someone
who roots for people

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:50.250
and want to see them do well.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:52.930
You really wanna be known as
someone who is judgemental

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:56.590
critical and generally disapproving
of the world around you

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:58.283
and all the people in it.

00:01:59.991 --> 00:02:01.991
(sighs)

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:05.643
Jared's a good guy.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:08.280
We all like Jared,

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.210
but he keeps on bringing
up his dead grandpa

00:02:10.210 --> 00:02:12.820
like all the time and
it's super depressing.

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:14.830
Really brings down the vibe.

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:16.950
Tip number three, be useless.

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.810
Never extend your hand
to help another person,

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:22.320
be incredibly stingy with your efforts

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:24.190
to contribute to the world around you

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:25.800
in any significant way.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.690
Look to weasel out of
work and responsibilities

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:30.970
as often as possible.

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:32.650
Let other people do the heavy lifting.

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:34.660
Say you have a talent
for playing the piano

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:36.680
and it's somebody's birthday
and you're at a party

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:38.657
and they say, "Joey, you
know how to play the piano?

00:02:38.657 --> 00:02:40.450
"Can you play happy birthday for us?"

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:41.283
That would be incredible.

00:02:41.283 --> 00:02:43.660
That would be so amazing.

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:44.493
Say no.

00:02:44.493 --> 00:02:46.130
Don't be generous with your gifts.

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:48.390
Don't shed positivity to other people.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:49.490
You're not a monkey.

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:50.640
This isn't the circus.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:53.260
Always keep your gifts
and talents to yourself.

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:55.410
Tip number four, be a pessimist.

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:57.850
One of the most important
traits you can have

00:02:57.850 --> 00:03:00.870
if you want to be somebody
who tremendously unlikable

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:02.190
is pessimism.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:04.120
You wanna suck the life out of the room.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.530
If you're part of a sports team,

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:07.010
somebody scores a nice goal.

00:03:07.010 --> 00:03:08.780
And they're in the
dressing room afterwards

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:11.557
talking about, "oh, what a
beautiful snipe that was,

00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:13.150
"dangled snipe Sally Boys."

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:15.477
You wanna be the person who says,

00:03:15.477 --> 00:03:16.787
"yeah, that wasn't that nice."

00:03:16.787 --> 00:03:18.690
"Like you could've gone top corner."

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:21.480
Somebody shows you a piece of
art they've been working on.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:23.350
Don't congratulate them if it's good,

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:24.810
explain how it can be better.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:26.800
Always be acutely aware of the fact

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:28.180
that things could be better.

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:29.810
Complain, complain, complain.

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:31.580
Holy shit it's so stupid.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.240
People are the worst drivers.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:36.120
Man, I was stuck in traffic
for 45 minutes today

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:37.220
it was brutal.

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:39.230
Excuse me, why is my coffee cold?

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:40.690
Oh, my back hurts.

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:43.000
Man, I just want to go home.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.180
Always find something to complain about.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:46.830
Call yourself a realist.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.660
But in reality, you're a pessimist.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.000
Tip number five, be close-minded.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.900
Assume that whatever
information that you have

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.460
in the present moment
is the gold standard.

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:59.100
It's better than whatever
anyone else has been told.

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:02.240
So when someone shares their
perspective on life with you

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:04.560
always have a cognitive bias against it.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:05.640
It's not what you think

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.080
so it's probably wrong.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.340
Assume that because you read it in a book

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:12.180
or watched it on the news,
that it must be true.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.290
Never create a space for dialogue.

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:16.900
Don't talk about the
nuances of a situation.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:19.280
Close yourself off to
that negative influence.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:21.030
Most people are sheep anyways.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:22.560
Don't let people influence you.

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:25.440
Psychologically lock
yourself into whatever belief

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:28.080
that you have and guard it with your life.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.610
Tip number six, develop a large ego.

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:34.280
Maintain a constant facade
that you are blameless

00:04:34.280 --> 00:04:35.120
and perfect.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:37.360
Never look at your situation objectively,

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:39.740
be blissfully unaware of your flaws.

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:43.130
And if you do find some
flaws, hide them at all costs.

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:45.180
You can't let people
know that you're human

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:46.630
and just like them.

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:47.590
You're perfect.

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:48.423
You're a god.

00:04:48.423 --> 00:04:50.070
A great way to make people feel

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:52.060
like they just can't get close to you

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:55.340
is to never show any kind of
weakness or vulnerability.

00:04:55.340 --> 00:04:58.120
This will help you not
be relatable whatsoever.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:01.110
Always build yourself
up and talk very highly

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:03.700
about yourself, and be
snappy and defensive

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:06.520
